{"kind":"assert","text":"Failed claims close a register. The second fact of 1f8fecbc holds on every register pin of CREATION_COHORTS that has a host: @5, @17, @18, @19, @20, @21, @23 and @24. It takes 64 found acts whose attempts fail, in one outage or added up over several. After that, every found gets type-full, and the host's return does not reopen the register. Please rule on the repair.\n\nHead 96212d60 records this as a test: packages/cli/test/failed-claims-close-register.defect.scope.test.ts, 15 of 15 pass, and I reran it at that head. Evidence: ~/play/artroom-evidence/2026-11-01-failed-claims/. The scopes, the CLI, the routes, the driver and the production artifactsOutside and gitHubOutside are real. The Artifacts binding, GitHub's fetch and the clock are scripted, and fixture drivers stand in for the alarm. No real outage ran, and no Worker was contacted.\n\nWhat ran:\n- A thrown Artifacts call, a GitHub network error, 503, 403 or a 422 gives unknown three times. Artifacts NOT_FOUND gives refused three times. So a real outage most likely gives unknown.\n- A fast failure uses all three attempts in 3 s on the scripted clock. A hung host uses them in 93 s, by a sum of steps and not observed. So a short outage is enough.\n- The claim stays pending with no repository, and the counts read 2 active, 64 pending.\n- One key can fill all 64. Under open, any key may sign, and no limit applies to found, which I read at object.ts:611. Under keys, only a listed founder can.\n- A rerun reuses the claim and makes no host call. --again spends a new place, and the old one stays held.\n- A missing host setting or binding sends no attempt. The claim holds its place and completes when the setting returns.\n\nWhat a person sees:\n- In the outage and on each rerun after it: \"Gave up waiting for the directory after 3 reads. What was asked may still take effect; ... or with --again to sign a new one, which creates a second repository.\" After three attempts the first sentence is false unless a late reply comes, and the second is false when the first claim made none.\n- At 64: \"Refused: type-full, judged at entry \u003cregister\u003e:262. The request was refused.\"\n- dap log register shows \"outcome; 1 effects, 0 sends\", with no failure.\n\nWhat frees a place: only a confirmed outcome, which needs the attempt's own reply. A hung attempt's late reply did free one in the run, and it lives in memory, so a restart loses it (read). A rerun, --again, a restart, a day, or the host's return frees nothing. No retry act, timed rule or operator act exists.\n\nThe operator cannot recover a closed register in place. The way out is a new register. Rooms that exist keep working.\n\nWho this reaches, from the wrangler files and docs and not from any Worker: dap-demo, public and open, on @17; dap-grow on @17; dap-lending on @5; dap-commons on @23. I have not read how many pending claims any of them holds. You can read that, and I ask you to, because a register near 64 changes the urgency. dap-demo matters most, because anyone can sign found there.\n\nRepair options:\nA. A final failed state set when the last attempt closes with nothing selected, with a late confirmed going to delete-repository. New pin. It reaches no existing register. Only this frees places on its own.\nB. A larger max or a per-key limit. New pin. It delays closure and frees nothing, so it is not enough alone.\nC. Longer backoff for create-repository, at object.ts:198. No pin. It helps only outages shorter than the new spacing, and spacing now covers every operation kind.\nD. Hold sends through Outside.ready after a failure until a probe succeeds. No pin, so it reaches deployed registers (read, not run). It needs a failure record and a wake. Places can still fill during an outage, and the attempts stay unsent, so those claims complete when the host returns.\nE. Correct the CLI words. No pin. The client still cannot read the claim's state.\n\nI recommend D and E now, then A in the next register pin. D stops most new loss on rooms that exist, and A is the lasting repair. No option recovers a register that is already full. Your cccd205a says one next cohort at a time, so A would join the slice that builds the token pin, unless you want it sooner.\n\nThe test names its cases DEFECT and pins today's behaviour. I hold that head until your ruling and land it with the repair, which turns those cases around.\n\nNot run: a directory that refuses create after repository is set, the real alarm path, a restart during a hung send, and any real host's rate limits. Under open on GitHub, a burst of found acts could trigger the 403 itself, and I only scripted that reply.\n\nThis also corrects the founder note's row \"pending, all three attempts used: can it go on? No\". That is wrong while an attempt is unknown and the sending object lives, because the late-reply case moved such a claim to active.","body":{"to":"20db43a245e9780b92a587425d387d393b17ffc90b89e036ff752399f88fc517"}}